{"1-4":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"galatia-g1053","name":"Galatia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":3}],"words":[{"base":"G3048","lemma":"λογία","tr":"logia","gloss":"collection","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"G1437","lemma":"ἐάν","tr":"ean","gloss":"if","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":336},{"base":"G3752","lemma":"ὅταν","tr":"hotan","gloss":"when(-ever)","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":123},{"base":"G4198","lemma":"πορεύω","tr":"poreuō","gloss":"to travel","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":147},{"base":"G1053","lemma":"Γαλατία","tr":"Galatia","gloss":"Galatia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2137","lemma":"εὐοδόω","tr":"euodoō","gloss":"to get along well","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G0667","lemma":"ἀποφέρω","tr":"apopherō","gloss":"to carry off","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G2343","lemma":"θησαυρίζω","tr":"thēsaurizō","gloss":"to store up","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G1473","lemma":"ἐγώ","tr":"egō","gloss":"I","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":841},{"base":"G1299","lemma":"διατάσσω","tr":"diatassō","gloss":"to direct","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":16}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2CO","chapter":9,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"For this ministry of service is not only supplying the needs of the saints, but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanksgiving to God.","from":1},{"book":"2CO","chapter":9,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Thanks be to God for His indescribable gift!","from":1},{"book":"ROM","chapter":12,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Share with the saints who are in need. Practice hospitality.","from":1},{"book":"2CO","chapter":8,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"Now, brothers, we want you to know about the grace that God has given the churches of Macedonia.","from":1},{"book":"2CO","chapter":8,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor, so that you through His poverty might become rich.","from":1},{"book":"1JN","chapter":3,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"If anyone with earthly possessions sees his brother in need, but withholds his compassion from him, how can the love of God abide in him?","from":1},{"book":"ROM","chapter":15,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Now, however, I am on my way to Jerusalem to serve the saints there.","from":1},{"book":"ROM","chapter":15,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"For Macedonia and Achaia were pleased to make a contribution for the poor among the saints in Jerusalem.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"5-12":{"people":[{"id":"timothy-g5095g","name":"Timothy","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"apollos-g0625","name":"Apollos","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12}],"places":[{"id":"macedonia-g3109","name":"Macedonia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"ephesus-g2181","name":"Ephesus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"words":[{"base":"G2064","lemma":"ἔρχομαι","tr":"erchomai","gloss":"to come","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":631},{"base":"G4314","lemma":"πρός","tr":"pros","gloss":"to","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":700},{"base":"G1063","lemma":"γάρ","tr":"gar","gloss":"for","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":1041},{"base":"G2443","lemma":"ἵνα","tr":"hina","gloss":"in order that","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":668},{"base":"G4311","lemma":"προπέμπω","tr":"propempō","gloss":"to help on the way","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"G1961","lemma":"ἐπιμένω","tr":"epimenō","gloss":"to remain","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"G3109","lemma":"Μακεδονία","tr":"Makedonia","gloss":"Macedonia","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"G1437","lemma":"ἐάν","tr":"ean","gloss":"if","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":336},{"base":"G0080","lemma":"ἀδελφός","tr":"adelphos","gloss":"brother","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":343},{"base":"G1330","lemma":"διέρχομαι","tr":"dierchomai","gloss":"to pass through","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":43}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2CO","chapter":2,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"Now when I went to Troas to preach the gospel of Christ and a door stood open for me in the Lord,","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":14,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"When they arrived, they gathered the church together and reported all that God had done through them, and how He had opened the door of faith to the Gentiles.","from":9},{"book":"COL","chapter":4,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"as you pray also for us, that God may open to us a door for the word, so that we may proclaim the mystery of Christ, for which I am in chains.","from":9},{"book":"REV","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"To the angel of the church in Philadelphia write: These are the words of the One who is holy and true, who holds the key of David. What He opens no one can shut, and what He shuts no one can open.","from":9},{"book":"REV","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"I know your deeds. Behold, I have placed before you an open door, which no one can shut. I know that you have only a little strength, yet you have kept My word and have not denied My name.","from":9},{"book":"2CO","chapter":1,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"We do not want you to be unaware, brothers, of the hardships we encountered in the province of Asia. We were under a burden far beyond our ability to endure, so that we despaired even of life.","from":9},{"book":"2CO","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"He has delivered us from such a deadly peril, and He will deliver us. In Him we have placed our hope that He will yet again deliver us,","from":9},{"book":"1TI","chapter":4,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Let no one despise your youth, but set an example for the believers in speech, in conduct, in love, in faith, in purity.","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2}]},"13-18":{"people":[{"id":"stephanas-g4734","name":"Stephanas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"achaicus-g0883","name":"Achaicus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"fortunatus-g5415","name":"Fortunatus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17}],"places":[{"id":"achaia-g0882","name":"Achaia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15}],"words":[{"base":"G4734","lemma":"Στεφανᾶς","tr":"Stephanas","gloss":"Stephanas","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"G5108","lemma":"τοιοῦτος","tr":"toioutos","gloss":"such as this","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":56},{"base":"G2901","lemma":"κραταιόω","tr":"krataioō","gloss":"to strengthen","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G4903","lemma":"συνεργέω","tr":"sunergeō","gloss":"to work with","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G0378","lemma":"ἀναπληρόω","tr":"anaplēroō","gloss":"to fulfil","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G5021","lemma":"τάσσω","tr":"tassō","gloss":"to appoint","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G0536","lemma":"ἀπαρχή","tr":"aparchē","gloss":"firstfruits","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"G4739","lemma":"στήκω","tr":"stēkō","gloss":"to stand","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"G5303","lemma":"ὑστέρημα","tr":"husterēma","gloss":"deficiency","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"G0882","lemma":"Ἀχαΐα","tr":"Achaia","gloss":"Achaia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":233,"source":"openbible","text":"Have I not commanded you to be strong and courageous? Do not be afraid; do not be discouraged, for the LORD your God is with you wherever you go.”","from":13},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":228,"source":"openbible","text":"Therefore take up the full armor of God, so that when the day of evil comes, you will be able to stand your ground, and having done everything, to stand.","from":13},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":228,"source":"both","text":"Pray in the Spirit at all times, with every kind of prayer and petition. To this end, stay alert with all perseverance in your prayers for all the saints.","from":13},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":179,"source":"openbible","text":"Finally, be strong in the Lord and in His mighty power.","from":13},{"book":"1CO","chapter":15,"verse":58,"verseEnd":58,"votes":152,"source":"both","text":"Therefore, my beloved brothers, be steadfast and immovable. Always excel in the work of the Lord, because you know that your labor in the Lord is not in vain.","from":13},{"book":"2CO","chapter":12,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":132,"source":"openbible","text":"But He said to me, “My grace is sufficient for you, for My power is perfected in weakness.” Therefore I will boast all the more gladly in my weaknesses, so that the power of Christ may rest on me.","from":13},{"book":"2CO","chapter":12,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":132,"source":"openbible","text":"That is why, for the sake of Christ, I delight in weaknesses, in insults, in hardships, in persecutions, in difficulties. For when I am weak, then I am strong.","from":13},{"book":"GAL","chapter":5,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":118,"source":"both","text":"It is for freedom that Christ has set us free. Stand firm, then, and do not be encumbered once more by a yoke of slavery.","from":13}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"19-24":{"people":[{"id":"aquila-g0207","name":"Aquila","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"priscilla-g4252","name":"Priscilla","kind":"person","brief":"Christian teacher","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"achaicus-g0883","name":"Achaicus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"fortunatus-g5415","name":"Fortunatus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"stephanas-g4734","name":"Stephanas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"timothy-g5095g","name":"Timothy","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"places":[{"id":"asia-g0773","name":"Asia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"corinth-g2882","name":"Corinth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"philippi-g5375","name":"Philippi","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"words":[{"base":"G0782","lemma":"ἀσπάζομαι","tr":"aspazomai","gloss":"to pay respects to","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":60},{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":714},{"base":"G1577","lemma":"ἐκκλησία","tr":"ekklēsia","gloss":"assembly","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":114},{"base":"G4251","lemma":"Πρίσκα","tr":"Priska","gloss":"Prisca","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G3326","lemma":"μετά","tr":"meta","gloss":"with","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":465},{"base":"G0207","lemma":"Ἀκύλας","tr":"Akulas","gloss":"Aquila","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G0331","lemma":"ἀνάθεμα","tr":"anathema","gloss":"devoted","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G5370","lemma":"φίλημα","tr":"philēma","gloss":"kiss","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"G0783","lemma":"ἀσπασμός","tr":"aspasmos","gloss":"salutation","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G2424","lemma":"Ἰησοῦς","tr":"Iēsous","gloss":"Jesus","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":911}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ROM","chapter":16,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Greet one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ send you greetings.","from":20},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Grace to all who love our Lord Jesus Christ with an undying love.","from":22},{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Whoever has My commandments and keeps them is the one who loves Me. The one who loves Me will be loved by My Father, and I will love him and reveal Myself to him.”","from":22},{"book":"ROM","chapter":16,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The God of peace will soon crush Satan under your feet. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.","from":23},{"book":"2CO","chapter":5,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"For Christʼs love compels us, because we are convinced that One died for all, therefore all died.","from":22},{"book":"2CO","chapter":5,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"And He died for all, that those who live should no longer live for themselves, but for Him who died for them and was raised again.","from":22},{"book":"MAT","chapter":10,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Anyone who loves his father or mother more than Me is not worthy of Me; anyone who loves his son or daughter more than Me is not worthy of Me;","from":22},{"book":"JHN","chapter":8,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Jesus said to them, “If God were your Father, you would love Me, for I have come here from God. I have not come on My own, but He sent Me.","from":22}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":5},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]}}